CMTypes/Algebra.lean
--------------------
New file (70f2e46): algebraic background for CM types. Line numbers as
of 2026-10-01 (commit 70f2e46).
[x] Algebra ℚ (center R)                                             (l.17–46)
      SMul, center_algebra_map and the Algebra instance are done.

[ ] IsSimpleRing_basechange                                          (l.58)
      F ⊗[K] R is simple. FALSE as stated (ℂ ⊗[ℝ] ℂ ≅ ℂ × ℂ): needs
      [Algebra.IsCentral K R] as well. Not in Mathlib (no IsSimpleRing /
      tensor product results at all). Standard proof: take an element of
      minimal length Σ aᵢ ⊗ bᵢ in a nonzero ideal and use simplicity +
      centrality to reduce it to 1 ⊗ b.

[ ] IsCentral_basechange                                             (l.62)
      Base change of a central algebra is central. Marked "does not look
      like it's needed". Also not in Mathlib (Algebra.IsCentral.left_of_tensor
      goes the other way).

[ ] fact₁ / dimension_IsSimple_algebra                               (l.65, l.81)
      Proved modulo IsSimpleRing_basechange, so they inherit its missing
      [Algebra.IsCentral K R] hypothesis. With it, finrank K R = n * n via
      Module.finrank_baseChange; the reduced degree could then be defined
      directly as Nat.sqrt (finrank K R) instead of via choose.
